  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "FD_IDENTITY_CAPTURE",
      "finding": "observe_fd reads metadata from the borrowed live File and records fd plus device/inode; no descriptor ownership is copied into the observation."
    },
    {
      "id": "ORIGINAL_SLOT_REJECTION",
      "finding": "assert_closed rejects the original observed slot when it still resolves to the original device/inode pair; only NotFound or a different pair is accepted; all other I/O errors fail."
    },
    {
      "id": "NEGATIVE_CONTROL",
      "name": "closure_probe_rejects_a_live_original_descriptor",
      "annotation": "#[should_panic(expected = \"original loader descriptor is still open\")]",
      "finding": "The original tempfile remains owned in scope during the probe. Unrelated creation/metadata/proc errors do not carry the expected assertion message and cannot stand in for the intended rejection."
    },
    {
      "id": "CFG_IMPORTS",
      "finding": "residency.rs gates sealed_loader with cfg(target_os = \"linux\"); tests are nested under cfg(test). MetadataExt is compatible with that Linux scope; File and io remain available through the existing super::* import."
    },
    {
      "id": "RAII_ERROR_PATH",
      "finding": "The unpublished memfd is owned by a local File, transferred into Vec<SealedMember> only after verification, and the bundle is returned only after the complete loop. The reviewed ? exits drop the current local File and all earlier Vec entries. No production source bytes changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "PRIOR_ASSERTIONS_PRESERVED",
      "finding": "The three existing corruption/cancellation/deadline tests change only their descriptor capture calls. Their existing error, complete-hash, usage, selection, and observed-count assertions are preserved."
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The reported M4 failure does not establish a production descriptor leak or prove that reuse was its actual cause; the old integer-slot oracle cannot distinguish those cases.",
    "The revised check observes the original integer slot and device/inode identity. It is not a proof of reclaiming all duplicated descriptors, mmap references, or downstream owners.",
    "The production documentation already excludes certification of every downstream reference or refund authority from bundle Drop.",
    "Device/inode equality is filesystem-object identity, not proof of a unique open-file-description. A later same-object reference may conservatively fail the probe.",
    "No compiler result, native rerun, daemon execution, FinalUse, or service acceptance is inferred from this static review.",
    "Non-membership in the curated authority/Root/W1 maps does not establish absence of whole-program or runtime dependencies."
  ],
